## 6. Frontend (Next.js static export) conventions

- **Output is 100% static.** No API routes, no server actions, no
  middleware. Every dynamic path ships with `generateStaticParams` +
  `dynamicParams = false`, so unknown slugs 404 at build time.
- **Trailing slashes everywhere.** `next.config.ts` sets
  `trailingSlash: true`; every `<Link>` href ends with `/`. Missing the
  slash serves a 404 through CloudFront.
- **Data access**: `app/lib/api.ts` wraps the public API with typed,
  fail-soft getters. Every request returns `null` on error so a flaky API
  can't break a build. For multi-page fetches, use
  `listAllDocumentSlugs` (capped at `MAX_STATIC_DOCS`, default 20 000).
- **Images**: `images: { unoptimized: true }` because `next/image`
  optimization doesn't work in static export.
- **Tailwind**: classic v3 setup (`tailwind.config.ts` + `postcss.config.mjs`).
  If you switch to v4/`@theme`, update this rule.
- **SEO**:
  - Every route exports `metadata` or `generateMetadata` with a canonical
    URL in `alternates.canonical`.
  - The `prebuild` script writes `public/sitemap.xml` and `public/robots.txt`
    from the live API — set `MAX_SITEMAP_DOCS` env var to trim if needed.
  - OpenGraph and Twitter metadata live in `app/layout.tsx` as defaults,
    overridden per page where it matters.
- **Styling language**: dark, FOIA-file tone — `bg-gray-950`, red-600
  accent for "Declassified." Keep cards flat, text mono for identifiers
  (NARA IDs, slugs), prose for paragraphs. Don't introduce a marketing
  gradient or rounded pills unless you're intentionally changing the look.

### 6.1 Build + deploy

```bash
cd frontend
npm ci
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://api.blackvaultdocs.com \
  MAX_STATIC_DOCS=20000 \
  npm run build      # also runs scripts/generate-sitemap.mjs via prebuild
aws s3 sync out/ s3://blackvaultdocs.com/ --delete \
  --cache-control "public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600"
aws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id E2I87T26ZZLVBA --paths '/*'
```

Only deploy from a laptop — the EC2 instance role can't touch CloudFront.

